To efficiently find the unique words in `Text1` that do not appear in `Text2`, you can use MATLAB's built-in functions `lower`, `strsplit`, `setdiff`, and `ismember`. Here is a more efficient implementation that handles large amounts of text:

```matlab
% Read texts from files
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt');
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt');

% Convert text to lowercase and split into words
words1 = strsplit(lower(text1), ' ');
words2 = strsplit(lower(text2), ' ');

% Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
uniqueWords = setdiff(setdiff(words1, words2), []);

% Remove empty strings (if any)
uniqueWords = uniqueWords(~cellfun(@isempty, uniqueWords));

% Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);
```

